# PiBuddyCam: let the unprivileged pibuddycam service account invoke ONLY the
# fixed-verb root helper (WP-R1, B3). A sudoers command listed without arguments
# permits any arguments, so /usr/libexec/pibuddycam/pibuddycam-priv validates the verb
# itself and exits 2 on anything it does not implement; nothing else is granted.
#
# Installed to /etc/sudoers.d/pibuddycam (root:root, mode 0440) and checked with
# `visudo -cf` during the image build.
#
# env_reset strips the caller's environment (so PIBUDDYCAM_APP_ROOT and PATH
# cannot be injected by the service account) and secure_path pins the PATH sudo
# uses for the helper. Both are sudo defaults, but stating them here keeps the
# privilege boundary independent of the base image's global sudoers.
Defaults:pibuddycam env_reset
Defaults:pibuddycam secure_path="/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin"
pibuddycam ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/pibuddycam/pibuddycam-priv
